# partial_eval: a partial evaluator from a function of planck to functions of vasm
# Copyright (C) 2026 nineties
#
# partial_eval.specialize(tree, args, rty) is the Module{[...]} of vasm for the function of the tree called with the arguments args; its result has the
# type rty. It always gives a module: what cannot be computed when specialize runs is left in the functions of vasm, as it is written.
# The module can be given to vasm_build.build; partial_eval.vasm_text(m) is its text and partial_eval.with_main(m, values) adds the function main that calls the first
# function with the values.
#
# The tree of a function is what a quasi-quote gives, such as `(pow(x, 0) := 1) or `({ even(n) := ...; odd(n) := ... }). The function that the
# last definition of the tree defines is the one that is specialized, and the others are the functions it calls. A tree of the form
# `(x -> e) is a function without a name.
#
# An argument Dyn{t} is an input that is known only when the result runs; it is a parameter of type t (a type of vasm) of the first function.
# Val{} is the type of any value of planck. Any other argument is a static value: everything that depends on static values only is computed
# when specialize runs, so what is left in the functions is the operations on the parameters. A static value may be a function: its tree is
# given as the value (twice(f, x) := f(f(x)) with `(x -> x + 1) for f). A value that Dyn marks is not given as a static value.
#
# The values that are left:
#   An integer or a bool that is the only kind in its place has the type I32{} (I64{} past 32 bits), Bool{} or that of the parameter it comes from.
#   A string has the type &static [u8] while it comes from a literal or a parameter.
#   Any other value is a val of vasm: a list or a constructed value, a function, an array, or a value that is of different kinds in different branches.
#   When a type does not hold what comes to it, the type becomes val and specialize starts again.
# The arrays (array(n), u8_array(n), u16_array(n), i32_array(n), and those in the static values) are arrays of val, since planck shares them.
# They are made and written when the result runs, in the order a planck program does them.
#
# A call is unfolded where it is written. A call to a function that is being unfolded, from inside a branch of an if whose condition is dynamic,
# is not unfolded: a function is made for the static arguments of the call (and made once for the same static arguments), and the call
# is a call of it. So pow with n = 3 is one function, and f(x, k) := if (x == k) x else f(x + 1, k) with k = 3 is a function that calls itself.
# The functions are named name_spec for the first and name_spec_1, name_spec_2, ... for the others, in the order they are made.
# When the call is made while a function is being made for the same function with other static arguments (the static arguments change at
# each call, as in f(n + 1, x - 1)), the arguments that differ are parameters of the function that is made, so the functions do not grow.
# The first function has the result rty, and another function of the same name too; the result of the others is rty until it does not hold their value, and then val.
#
# A variable that is assigned under a dynamic condition or in a loop that is left is a register of the function. A variable that a function value
# shares with the place it was made is an array of one element. A while whose condition is static runs when specialize runs, at most
# loop_limit rounds; the rest of it is left.
#
# A built-in function with a dynamic argument calls its implementation of vasm/builtins.pk. Printing, reading and writing are always left, in
# the order of the program; a function of the standard libraries is unfolded from its source when an argument is dynamic or a function.
# Any other function that is not in the tree is called when specialize runs.
#
# handle and perform: when the perform is reached with no dynamic condition between it and the handle, the handler runs where it is, with
# its continuation. When there is a dynamic condition between them, the handler runs where the perform is: a handler that does not
# use its continuation ends the handle, and one that gives a value to it in the end (k(v) last) goes on. What is left to do in the other
# path of the condition is in the else part.
#
# What cannot be left as an operation of vasm stops the result when it is reached, with a message to the error output (stop):
# eval, parse, load and the like with a dynamic argument, a function that is not in the tree or the libraries with a dynamic argument, a perform
# whose handle is outside the function that is made, and a continuation that is used otherwise than above across a dynamic condition.

use("base")
use("list")
use("table")
use("string")
use("vasm/check")
use("vasm/builtins")
use("vasm/text")

module partial_eval {

text_of_vasm := vasm_text.text

fun pe_eval
fun values
fun call_named
fun call_value
fun unfold
fun make_fn
fun residual_call
fun primitive
fun box
fun box_fun
fun coerce
fun dyn_if
fun stop
fun pe_while
fun lift
fun eq_op
fun has_array
fun add_escapes
fun close
fun close_gone
fun take_defs
fun same_env
fun close_opens
fun box_closure
fun val_of_function
fun arity_known
fun loc_dy
fun assigns_into
fun specialize_once
fun set_reg_call
fun eq_test
fun static_match

# === State ===
# the functions of the tree: name -> the list of the clauses Lambda{Tuple{p, ...}, body}
pe_defs := table.new()
# the variables, the statements (the last first) and the registers of the function that is being made
decls := []
pe_stmts := []
count := 0
# the number of the branches of dynamic conditions around the code, and the functions being unfolded: Tuple{key, depth}, the last first
depth := 0
pe_stack := []
# the conditions around the code: Fr{depth, a one-element array of the statements to put before the condition}, the innermost first
frames := []
# the if statements whose else part is being written: Op{statements before, condition, statements of the path that left, frame}
opens := []
# the handlers of the function being made, the innermost first, the loops around the code, the handles left from a branch, the Defs in a branch
handlers := []
loops := []
escapes := []
deflog := []
# the bodies of the functions being unfolded
bodies := []
# the type of the results, the first function, the functions made (the last first), what they were made for, and the built-in functions called
pe_rty := Unit{}
entry := ""
entry_fv := none
pe_fns := []
memo := []
impls := []
nres := 0
nids := 0
nhandles := 0
# the functions being made: Tuple{key of the function, template}, the last first
making := []
# the names and the functions whose type has become val, and the variables that are registers in any loop: they stay over the starts of specialize
force := table.new()
pe_at := Pos{0}
first_key := none
root := none

# the rounds of a while with a static condition that run when specialize runs
loop_limit := 64

# === Values ===
# A static value is a value of planck, or a function: Cl{clauses, id} for a function made here, whose clauses are Tuple{lambda, environment},
# Fv{name} for one in the tree, Pr{name} for a built-in or another global function, Kn{...} for a continuation.
# A dynamic value is Dy{name, type}, a variable of the function that is made. A constructed value may have dynamic values in it.
# A location of a variable holds a value, or Mt{register, type} for a register that is assigned, or Ce{array} for an array of one element.

pe_dyn(v) := typeof(v) == 'mexpr and head(v) == 'Dy
marker(v) := typeof(v) == 'mexpr and head(v) == 'Dyn
pe_fun(v) := typeof(v) == 'mexpr and member(head(v), ['Cl, 'Fv, 'Pr, 'Kn, 'Ki])
is_mexpr(v) := typeof(v) == 'mexpr and not pe_dyn(v) and not pe_fun(v)
# v has a dynamic value or a function in it, so it is not a value of planck that a function of planck takes
opaque(v) := pe_dyn(v) or pe_fun(v) or (typeof(v) == 'mexpr and list.any(opaque, vasm_tlist(v)))
is_bool(v) := v == true or v == false
int_type(t) := vasm_check.int(t)
static_ref := Ref{'shr, 'static, Arr{U8{}}}
val_dy(v) := pe_dyn(v) and arg(v, 1) == Val{}
bool_dy(v) := pe_dyn(v) and arg(v, 1) == Bool{}
int_dy(v) := pe_dyn(v) and vasm_check.int(arg(v, 1))
ref_dy(v) := pe_dyn(v) and head(arg(v, 1)) == 'Ref

# the integer v is in the range of i32. The value is divided, so that nothing depends on the size of an integer of planck.
fits_i32(v) := {
    n := if (v < 0) 0 - v else v
    n / 65536 < 32768
}

# the type that holds v when it is a value of the kind that a register of a scalar holds, and else val
kind_type(v) := if (pe_dyn(v)) arg(v, 1)
    else if (typeof(v) == 'int) (if (fits_i32(v)) I32{} else I64{})
    else if (is_bool(v)) Bool{}
    else if (typeof(v) == 'string) static_ref
    else Val{}

pe_join(a, b) := if (a == b) a
    else if (vasm_check.int(a) and vasm_check.int(b)) (if (a == I64{} or b == I64{}) I64{} else a)
    else Val{}

# a place of type t holds v without a check when the program runs
fits(v, t) := t == Val{} or pe_join(kind_type(v), t) == t

# === Environments ===
pe_env(parent) := En{table.new(), parent, table.new(), depth}
env_vals(e) := arg(e, 0)
env_parent(e) := arg(e, 1)
env_depths(e) := arg(e, 2)
env_born(e) := arg(e, 3)

pe_loc(env, x) := {
    e := env
    found := none
    while (found == none and e != none) {
        if (table.get(env_vals(e), x, Unbound{}) != Unbound{}) found = e
        else e = env_parent(e)
    }
    found
}

# x := v in env
def(env, x, v) := {
    if (depth > env_born(env)) deflog = Tuple{env, x, table.get(env_vals(env), x, Unbound{})} :: deflog
    table.set(env_vals(env), x, v)
    table.set(env_depths(env), x, depth)
}

# === Statements ===
fresh(t) := {
    count = count + 1
    x := intern(f"t{count}")
    decls = Decl{pe_at, x, t} :: decls
    x
}

emit(s) := {
    pe_stmts = s :: pe_stmts
}

assign(t, r) := {
    x := fresh(t)
    emit(Assign{pe_at, x, r})
    Dy{x, t}
}

# the value of the statements that fn() emits, and these statements
capture(fn) := {
    saved := pe_stmts
    pe_stmts = []
    v := fn()
    s := reverse(pe_stmts)
    pe_stmts = saved
    Tuple{s, v}
}

in_range(v) := v >= -32768 and v <= 32767

# the register of type t with the integer v, which is out of the range of a literal
big(v, t) := {
    x := fresh(t)
    n := if (v < 0) 0 - v else v
    ds := []
    while (n > 0) {
        ds = n % 32768 :: ds
        n = n / 32768
    }
    emit(Assign{pe_at, x, Mov{Imm{pe_at, 0}}})
    for (d in ds) {
        emit(Assign{pe_at, x, Bin{'shl, Reg{pe_at, x}, Imm{pe_at, 15}}})
        emit(Assign{pe_at, x, Bin{'bit_or, Reg{pe_at, x}, Imm{pe_at, d}}})
    }
    if (v < 0) emit(Assign{pe_at, x, Bin{'sub, Imm{pe_at, 0}, Reg{pe_at, x}}})
    Dy{x, t}
}

# the operand of the value v: a dynamic value, a bool, an integer or a string
operand(v) := if (pe_dyn(v)) Reg{pe_at, arg(v, 0)}
    else if (typeof(v) == 'int) (if (in_range(v)) Imm{pe_at, v} else Reg{pe_at, arg(big(v, I64{}), 0)})
    else if (is_bool(v)) Imm{pe_at, v}
    else if (typeof(v) == 'string) Str{pe_at, v}
    else Reg{pe_at, arg(box(v), 0)}

# the dynamic value v with the type t, converted if it has another integer type
to(v, t) := if (pe_dyn(v) and arg(v, 1) != t and vasm_check.int(arg(v, 1)) and vasm_check.int(t)) assign(t, Conv{pe_at, Reg{pe_at, arg(v, 0)}, t})
    else if (typeof(v) == 'int and vasm_check.int(t) and not in_range(v)) big(v, t)
    else v

# the value that a register of type t holds on a path that does not go on
dummy(t) := if (vasm_check.int(t)) 0 else if (t == Bool{}) false else if (t == Val{}) none else if (t == static_ref) "" else none

# a statement for a place of type t with a value on a path that does not go on
dummy_op(t) := if (t == Val{}) Sym{pe_at, 'none} else operand(dummy(t))

# x = v for the register x of type t
set_reg(x, t, v) := emit(Assign{pe_at, x, Mov{operand(coerce(v, t))}})

# a call of the function f of vasm/builtins.pk with the operands; its result has the type t (Unit{} for none)
impl_call(f, args, t) := {
    if (not member(f, impls)) impls = f :: impls
    if (t == Unit{}) {
        emit(CallS{pe_at, f, args})
        none
    } else assign(t, Call{pe_at, f, args})
}

# the result ends here when it runs, with the message; the value is what the place expects to go on
stop(msg) := {
    impl_call('v_stop, [Str{pe_at, msg}], Unit{})
    none
}

# === Values of val ===
# the value v as a val, in a register or as a symbol
box_op(v) := if (typeof(v) == 'symbol) Sym{pe_at, v} else Reg{pe_at, arg(box(v), 0)}

box(v) := if (val_dy(v)) v
    else if (pe_dyn(v)) assign(Val{}, Conv{pe_at, Reg{pe_at, arg(v, 0)}, Val{}})
    else if (typeof(v) == 'int) (if (in_range(v)) assign(Val{}, Conv{pe_at, Imm{pe_at, v}, Val{}}) else box(big(v, I64{})))
    else if (typeof(v) == 'string) assign(Val{}, Conv{pe_at, Str{pe_at, v}, Val{}})
    else if (typeof(v) == 'symbol) assign(Val{}, Mov{Sym{pe_at, v}})
    else if (pe_fun(v)) box_fun(v)
    else if (typeof(v) == 'mexpr) {
        ops := map(box_op, vasm_tlist(v))
        assign(Val{}, Con{pe_at, head(v), ops})
    } else if (typeof(v) == 'array or typeof(v) == 'plain) box(lift(v))
    else {
        stop("a function of planck that has no name is a value that is not left in vasm")
        assign(Val{}, Mov{Sym{pe_at, 'none}})
    }

# an array in the value v is made when the result runs: the value is the same with these arrays dynamic
lift(v) := if (typeof(v) == 'array or typeof(v) == 'plain) {
    n := if (typeof(v) == 'array) array_len(v) else plain_len(v)
    x := impl_call(if (typeof(v) == 'array) 'v_array else 'v_plain_array, [box_op(n)], Val{})
    i := 0
    while (i < n) {
        e := lift(if (typeof(v) == 'array) array_get(v, i) else plain_get(v, i))
        if (e != none and e != 0) impl_call('v_index_set, [Reg{pe_at, arg(x, 0)}, box_op(i), box_op(e)], Val{})
        i = i + 1
    }
    x
} else if (is_mexpr(v) and has_array(v)) foldl((t, x) -> push(t, x), mexpr(head(v), Tuple{}), map(lift, vasm_tlist(v)))
else v

has_array(v) := typeof(v) == 'array or typeof(v) == 'plain or (is_mexpr(v) and list.any(has_array, vasm_tlist(v)))

# the value v in a place of type t. A val that is to be another type is checked when the program runs.
coerce(v, t) := if (t == Val{}) box(v)
    else if (val_dy(v)) {
        if (vasm_check.int(t) or t == Bool{} or t == Own{Arr{U8{}}}) assign(t, Conv{pe_at, Reg{pe_at, arg(v, 0)}, t})
        else {
            stop("a val is not converted to the type of the result")
            dummy(t)
        }
    } else if (fits(v, t) or (int_dy(v) and vasm_check.int(t))) to(v, t)
    else if (vasm_check.int(t) or t == Bool{} or t == Own{Arr{U8{}}}) coerce(box(v), t)
    else {
        stop("a value is not converted to the type of the result")
        dummy(t)
    }

# === Starting again ===
# what is named by key is held by val from now on
widen(key) := {
    table.set(force, key, true)
    perform PeRestart{}
}

forced(key) := table.get(force, key, false)

# === The trees of functions ===
# a clause is Do{Declare{f}, Set{f, Fusion{f, Lambda{...}}}}
is_clause(t) := typeof(t) == 'mexpr and head(t) == 'Do and arity(t) == 2 and typeof(arg(t, 0)) == 'mexpr and head(arg(t, 0)) == 'Declare
is_def_tree(t) := is_clause(t) or (typeof(t) == 'mexpr and head(t) == 'Do and arity(t) > 0 and list.all(is_def_tree, vasm_tlist(t)))
is_fun_tree(t) := typeof(t) == 'mexpr and (head(t) == 'Lambda or is_def_tree(t))

# add the clauses of the tree t to pe_defs and give the name of the function of the last clause
load_tree(t) := if (is_clause(t)) match t {
    Do{Declare{f}, Set{_, Fusion{_, l}}} -> {
        table.set(pe_defs, f, append(table.get(pe_defs, f, []), [l]))
        f
    }
} else {
    last := none
    for (x in vasm_tlist(t)) last = load_tree(x)
    last
}

new_id() := {
    nids = nids + 1
    nids
}

# the function the tree t stands for
fun_value(t) := if (head(t) == 'Lambda) Cl{[Tuple{t, root}], new_id()} else Fv{load_tree(t)}

# === The functions of the standard libraries ===
# name -> the clauses, read from the source when a call needs them
lib_defs := none

lib_add(f, t) := if (typeof(t) == 'mexpr) match t {
    Lambda{_, _} -> table.set(lib_defs, f, append(table.get(lib_defs, f, []), [t]))
  | Fusion{a, b} -> {
        lib_add(f, a)
        lib_add(f, b)
    }
  | _ -> none
}

fun note_module
note_top(e) := if (typeof(e) == 'mexpr) match e {
    Do{Declare{f}, Set{_, t}} -> lib_add(f, t)
  | Set{f, t} -> lib_add(f, t)
  | Def{_, Apply{Lambda{Tuple{}, body}, Tuple{}}} -> note_module(body)
  | Def{f, t} -> lib_add(f, t)
  | _ -> none
}

# the functions defined in the body of a module are noted by the names they have in the body
note_module(body) := if (typeof(body) == 'mexpr and head(body) == 'Do) {
    for (s in vasm_tlist(body)) {
        if (is_clause(s)) note_top(s)
        else if (typeof(s) == 'mexpr and head(s) == 'Do) note_module(s)
        else note_top(s)
    }
}

read_lib(path, parser) := {
    s := read_file(path)
    go := true
    while (go) {
        r := parser(s)
        e := arg(r, 0)
        if (e == Eof{} or (typeof(e) == 'mexpr and head(e) == 'SyntaxError)) go = false
        else {
            note_top(e)
            s = arg(r, 1)
        }
    }
}

lib_clauses(f) := {
    if (lib_defs == none) {
        lib_defs = table.new()
        read_lib("planck/init.pk", parse_mexpr)
        for (n in ["list", "string", "base"]) read_lib(f"planck/lib/{n}.pk", parse)
    }
    table.get(lib_defs, f, none)
}

# list.f, string.f and base.f call the function f of the library
lib_callee(env, f) := if (typeof(f) == 'mexpr and head(f) == 'Apply and arg(f, 0) == '_record_get) {
    m := arg(arg(f, 1), 0)
    n := arg(arg(f, 1), 1)
    if (member(m, ['list, 'string, 'base]) and pe_loc(env, m) == none and typeof(n) == 'mexpr and head(n) == 'Quote) arg(n, 0) else f
} else f

# === Operations on dynamic values ===
pe_ops := [Tuple{'_add, 'add}, Tuple{'_sub, 'sub}, Tuple{'_mul, 'mul}, Tuple{'_div, 'div}, Tuple{'_quo, 'div}, Tuple{'_mod, 'rem},
    Tuple{'_eq, 'eq}, Tuple{'_ne, 'ne}, Tuple{'_lt, 'lt}, Tuple{'_le, 'le}, Tuple{'_gt, 'gt}, Tuple{'_ge, 'ge},
    Tuple{'bit_and, 'bit_and}, Tuple{'bit_or, 'bit_or}, Tuple{'bit_xor, 'bit_xor}, Tuple{'bit_shl, 'shl}, Tuple{'bit_sar, 'shr}]
cmps := ['_eq, '_ne, '_lt, '_le, '_gt, '_ge]

fun floor_op

# the integer of v for an operation: a val is read as i64
num(v) := if (val_dy(v)) assign(I64{}, Conv{pe_at, Reg{pe_at, arg(v, 0)}, I64{}}) else v

is_num(v) := typeof(v) == 'int or int_dy(v)

# the operation f on the values a and b, one of which is dynamic
dyn_op(f, a0, b0) := if (f == '_eq or f == '_ne) eq_op(f, a0, b0)
else {
    o := find(p -> arg(p, 0) == f, pe_ops)
    a := num(a0)
    b := num(b0)
    if (not is_num(a) or not is_num(b)) {
        stop(f"{symname(f)}: integer is expected")
        0
    } else {
        t := if (pe_dyn(a) and pe_dyn(b)) pe_join(arg(a, 1), arg(b, 1)) else if (pe_dyn(a)) arg(a, 1) else arg(b, 1)
        a2 := to(a, t)
        b2 := to(b, t)
        rt := if (member(f, cmps)) Bool{} else t
        if (f == '_quo or f == '_mod) floor_op(f, a2, b2, t) else assign(rt, Bin{arg(o, 1), operand(a2), operand(b2)})
    }
}

# a // b and a % b round toward minus infinity, while the operations div and rem of vasm round toward 0.
# m is -1 when the remainder r is not 0 and r and b differ in sign, and 0 otherwise.
# The quotient is then q + m and the remainder is r + (m & b).
floor_op(f, a, b, t) := {
    k := Imm{pe_at, if (t == I64{}) 63 else 31}
    q := assign(t, Bin{'div, operand(a), operand(b)})
    r := assign(t, Bin{'rem, operand(a), operand(b)})
    x := assign(t, Bin{'bit_xor, operand(r), operand(b)})
    m1 := assign(t, Bin{'shr, operand(x), k})
    n := assign(t, Bin{'sub, Imm{pe_at, 0}, operand(r)})
    o := assign(t, Bin{'bit_or, operand(n), operand(r)})
    m2 := assign(t, Bin{'shr, operand(o), k})
    m := assign(t, Bin{'bit_and, operand(m1), operand(m2)})
    if (f == '_quo) assign(t, Bin{'add, operand(q), operand(m)})
    else {
        c := assign(t, Bin{'bit_and, operand(m), operand(b)})
        assign(t, Bin{'add, operand(r), operand(c)})
    }
}

# a == b or a != b: on integers and bools as the operation of vasm, and on any other values as the operation on val
eq_op(f, a, b) := {
    op := if (f == '_eq) 'eq else 'ne
    if ((is_num(a) and is_num(b)) or ((bool_dy(a) or is_bool(a)) and (bool_dy(b) or is_bool(b)))) {
        t := if (pe_dyn(a) and pe_dyn(b)) pe_join(arg(a, 1), arg(b, 1)) else if (pe_dyn(a)) arg(a, 1) else arg(b, 1)
        assign(Bool{}, Bin{op, operand(to(a, t)), operand(to(b, t))})
    } else if (is_mexpr(a) and is_mexpr(b)) {
        # the shapes are known: only the parts that are dynamic are left
        same := if (head(a) != head(b) or arity(a) != arity(b)) false else {
            r := true
            i := 0
            while (i < arity(a)) {
                x := arg(a, i)
                y := arg(b, i)
                e := if (opaque(x) or opaque(y)) eq_op('_eq, x, y) else x == y
                if (r == true) r = e
                else if (r != false and e != true) {
                    if (e == false) r = false
                    else r = dyn_if(r, () -> e, () -> false)
                }
                i = i + 1
            }
            r
        }
        if (f == '_eq) same else if (pe_dyn(same)) primitive('_not, [same]) else not same
    } else if ((is_num(a) and (typeof(b) == 'string or is_mexpr(b) or bool_dy(b) or is_bool(b) or pe_fun(b))) or (is_num(b) and (typeof(a) == 'string or is_mexpr(a) or bool_dy(a) or is_bool(a) or pe_fun(a)))) f != '_eq
    else {
        x := box_op(a)
        y := box_op(b)
        assign(Bool{}, Bin{op, x, y})
    }
}

dyn_not(v) := if (bool_dy(v)) assign(Bool{}, Bin{'eq, operand(v), Imm{pe_at, false}})
    else if (val_dy(v)) assign(Bool{}, Bin{'eq, operand(v), Sym{pe_at, 'false}})
    else false

# a condition: only false is false. The value is true, false or a dynamic bool.
truth(v) := if (bool_dy(v)) v
    else if (val_dy(v)) assign(Bool{}, Bin{'ne, operand(v), Sym{pe_at, 'false}})
    else if (v == false) false
    else true

# === The built-in functions ===
# the functions that take any values in vasm/builtins.pk: Tuple{function of planck, function of vasm}
impl_table := [Tuple{'print, 'v_print}, Tuple{'put, 'v_put}, Tuple{'exit, 'v_exit},
    Tuple{'read_file, 'v_read_file}, Tuple{'try_read_file, 'v_try_read_file}, Tuple{'read_bytes, 'v_read_bytes}, Tuple{'write_file, 'v_write_file},
    Tuple{'strlen, 'v_strlen}, Tuple{'ord, 'v_ord}, Tuple{'substr, 'v_substr}, Tuple{'_strcat, 'v_strcat}, Tuple{'_to_text, 'v_to_text},
    Tuple{'head, 'v_head}, Tuple{'arity, 'v_arity}, Tuple{'arg, 'v_arg}, Tuple{'typeof, 'v_typeof}, Tuple{'intern, 'v_intern}, Tuple{'symname, 'v_symname},
    Tuple{'push, 'v_push}, Tuple{'mexpr, 'v_mexpr}, Tuple{'hash, 'v_hash},
    Tuple{'array, 'v_array}, Tuple{'u8_array, 'v_plain_array}, Tuple{'u16_array, 'v_plain_array}, Tuple{'i32_array, 'v_plain_array},
    Tuple{'array_get, 'v_arg}, Tuple{'plain_get, 'v_arg}, Tuple{'array_len, 'v_arity}, Tuple{'plain_len, 'v_arity},
    Tuple{'array_set, 'v_array_set}, Tuple{'plain_set, 'v_array_set}, Tuple{'_index_get, 'v_index_get}, Tuple{'_index_set, 'v_index_set},
    Tuple{'argv, 'v_argv}]

# the built-in functions that are left whatever their arguments are, since they read or write something outside or make an array
always := ['println, 'print, 'put, 'read_file, 'try_read_file, 'read_bytes, 'write_file, 'exit, 'array, 'u8_array, 'u16_array, 'i32_array, 'argv]

# the numbers of arguments of the built-in functions, for a built-in function that is a value
arity_of(f) := if (member(f, ['_add, '_sub, '_mul, '_div, '_quo, '_mod, '_lt, '_le, '_gt, '_ge, '_eq, '_ne, 'ord, 'arg, 'push, 'mexpr, 'array_get, 'plain_get, '_strcat, '_index_get, 'write_file])) 2
    else if (member(f, ['substr, 'array_set, 'plain_set, '_index_set])) 3
    else if (f == 'argv) 0
    else 1

pe_println(v) := if (typeof(v) == 'string) impl_call('println_str, [Str{pe_at, v}], Unit{})
    else if (ref_dy(v)) impl_call('println_str, [operand(v)], Unit{})
    else if (is_num(v)) impl_call('println_int, [operand(to(v, I64{}))], Unit{})
    else {
        impl_call('v_println, [box_op(v)], Val{})
        none
    }

# argv()[i] and array_len(argv())
argv_get(i) := if (is_num(i) or val_dy(i)) assign(static_ref, Call{pe_at, 'argv, [operand(to(num(i), I64{}))]})
    else {
        stop("the index of argv() is not an integer")
        ""
    }

pe_argc() := assign(I64{}, Call{pe_at, 'argc, []})

argv_call(e) := typeof(e) == 'mexpr and head(e) == 'Apply and arg(e, 0) == 'argv and arity(arg(e, 1)) == 0

# the function f of the host called with the static values vs; an array in the result is made when the result runs
host(f, vs) := {
    q := map(v -> mexpr('Quote, Tuple{v}), vs)
    lift(eval(mexpr('Apply, Tuple{f, foldl((t, x) -> push(t, x), Tuple{}, q)})))
}

call_impl(impl, vs) := impl_call(impl, map(box_op, vs), Val{})

# the registers of the function being made that hold an array that it has made: a[i] and a[i] = v on them are the statements of vasm
arrays := []
known_array(v) := val_dy(v) and member(arg(v, 0), arrays)
index_op(i) := operand(to(num(i), I64{}))

# array(n), u8_array(n), ... with an integer n
array_new(f, n) := {
    x := assign(Val{}, Call{pe_at, 'array, [index_op(n), if (f == 'array) Sym{pe_at, 'none} else box_op(0)]})
    arrays = arg(x, 0) :: arrays
    x
}

# for (x in xs) body with a list that is not known or a function that is left: a loop where the call is
for_tree := `({
    pe_for_i := pe_for_xs
    while (pe_for_i != Nil{}) {
        pe_for_f(arg(pe_for_i, 0))
        pe_for_i = arg(pe_for_i, 1)
    }
    none
})
pe_for(xs, fn) := {
    env := pe_env(root)
    def(env, 'pe_for_xs, xs)
    def(env, 'pe_for_f, fn)
    pe_eval(env, for_tree)
}

primitive(f, vs) := {
    dyn := list.any(opaque, vs)
    op := find(p -> arg(p, 0) == f, pe_ops)
    impl := find(p -> arg(p, 0) == f, impl_table)
    if (f == 'println and length(vs) == 1) {
        pe_println(vs[0])
        none
    } else if (not dyn and not member(f, always)) host(f, vs)
    else if (f == 'peg_for and length(vs) == 2) pe_for(vs[0], vs[1])
    else if (f == 'arg and is_mexpr(vs[0]) and typeof(vs[1]) == 'int) arg(vs[0], vs[1])
    else if (f == 'head and is_mexpr(vs[0])) head(vs[0])
    else if (f == 'arity and is_mexpr(vs[0])) arity(vs[0])
    else if (f == 'typeof and not val_dy(vs[0])) (if (pe_fun(vs[0])) 'function else if (is_mexpr(vs[0])) 'mexpr else if (int_dy(vs[0])) 'int else if (bool_dy(vs[0])) 'symbol else 'string)
    else if (f == 'strlen and ref_dy(vs[0])) impl_call('strlen, [operand(vs[0])], I32{})
    else if (f == '_not and length(vs) == 1) dyn_not(vs[0])
    else if (op != none and length(vs) == 2) dyn_op(f, vs[0], vs[1])
    else if (member(f, ['array, 'u8_array, 'u16_array, 'i32_array]) and length(vs) == 1 and (is_num(vs[0]) or val_dy(vs[0]))) array_new(f, vs[0])
    else if (f == 'array_get or f == 'plain_get or (f == '_index_get and length(vs) == 2 and known_array(vs[0]))) assign(Val{}, Index{pe_at, arg(box(vs[0]), 0), index_op(vs[1])})
    else if ((f == 'array_set or f == 'plain_set or f == '_index_set) and length(vs) == 3 and (f != '_index_set or known_array(vs[0]))) {
        i := index_op(vs[1])
        emit(IStore{pe_at, arg(box(vs[0]), 0), i, box_op(vs[2])})
        vs[2]
    }
    else if (f == 'exit and length(vs) == 1) {
        call_impl('v_exit, vs)
        none
    } else if (member(f, ['print, 'put]) and length(vs) == 1) {
        call_impl(arg(impl, 1), vs)
        none
    } else if (f == 'write_file or f == '_index_set or f == 'array_set or f == 'plain_set) {
        call_impl(arg(impl, 1), vs)
        vs[length(vs) - 1]
    } else if (impl != none) call_impl(arg(impl, 1), vs)
    else {
        cs := lib_clauses(f)
        if (cs != none) {
            table.set(pe_defs, f, cs)
            call_named(f, vs)
        } else {
            stop(f"{symname(f)} with a value known only when the program runs is not left in vasm")
            none
        }
    }
}

# === Patterns ===

# v is of the type shown by typeof: true, false or a dynamic bool
type_test(v, ty) := if (val_dy(v)) assign(Bool{}, Bin{'eq, Reg{pe_at, arg(assign(Val{}, Call{pe_at, 'typeof, [operand(v)]}), 0)}, Sym{pe_at, ty}})
    else if (pe_dyn(v)) (if (vasm_check.int(arg(v, 1))) ty == 'int else if (arg(v, 1) == Bool{}) ty == 'symbol else ty == 'string)
    else if (pe_fun(v)) ty == 'function
    else if (typeof(v) == 'mexpr) ty == 'mexpr
    else typeof(v) == ty

# the static a and then the value of fn(), which is emitted only when a holds
pe_and(a, fn) := if (a == false) false
    else if (a == true) fn()
    else {
        c := capture(fn)
        if (arg(c, 0) == [] and arg(c, 1) == true) a
        else dyn_if(a, () -> {
            for (s in arg(c, 0)) emit(s)
            arg(c, 1)
        }, () -> false)
    }

# the pattern p matches the value v: true, false or a dynamic bool. Only the test is emitted; bind gives the variables.
fun pe_test
test_args(p, v, i) := if (i >= arity(p)) true else {
    a := if (val_dy(v)) assign(Val{}, Index{pe_at, arg(v, 0), Imm{pe_at, i}}) else arg(v, i)
    pe_and(pe_test(arg(p, i), a), () -> test_args(p, v, i + 1))
}

pe_test(p, v) := {
    t := typeof(p)
    if (t == 'symbol) (if (p == true or p == false or p == none) eq_test(p, v) else true)
    else if (t == 'int or t == 'string) eq_test(p, v)
    else if (head(p) == 'Quote) eq_test(arg(p, 0), v)
    else if (head(p) == '_TypeOf) pe_and(type_test(v, arg(p, 1)), () -> pe_test(arg(p, 0), v))
    else if (val_dy(v)) {
        c := assign(Bool{}, Call{pe_at, 'is, [operand(v), Sym{pe_at, head(p)}, Imm{pe_at, arity(p)}]})
        if (list.all(q -> typeof(q) == 'symbol and not (q == true or q == false or q == none), vasm_tlist(p))) c
        else pe_and(c, () -> test_args(p, v, 0))
    } else if (not is_mexpr(v) or head(p) != head(v) or arity(p) != arity(v)) false
    else test_args(p, v, 0)
}

# the constant c and the value v are equal
eq_test(c, v) := if (opaque(v)) eq_op('_eq, c, v) else c == v

# bind the variables of the pattern p, which has matched v, in env
bind(env, p, v) := {
    t := typeof(p)
    if (t == 'symbol) {
        if (p != '_ and p != true and p != false and p != none) {
            table.set(env_vals(env), p, v)
            table.set(env_depths(env), p, depth)
        }
    } else if (t == 'int or t == 'string or head(p) == 'Quote) none
    else if (head(p) == '_TypeOf) bind(env, arg(p, 0), v)
    else {
        i := 0
        while (i < arity(p)) {
            q := arg(p, i)
            if (not (typeof(q) == 'symbol and (q == '_ or q == true or q == false or q == none)) and not (typeof(q) == 'int or typeof(q) == 'string)) {
                a := if (val_dy(v)) assign(Val{}, Index{pe_at, arg(v, 0), Imm{pe_at, i}}) else arg(v, i)
                bind(env, q, a)
            }
            i = i + 1
        }
    }
}

# === Evaluation ===

# the values of the expressions es, evaluated from the first, as the program does
values(env, es) := {
    n := arity(es)
    out := []
    i := 0
    while (i < n) {
        out = pe_eval(env, arg(es, i)) :: out
        i = i + 1
    }
    reverse(out)
}

# the clauses cs (Tuple{lambda, environment}) called with the values vs: the first clause that matches is unfolded. A test that depends on a
# dynamic value is left, and the other clauses are in its else part.
try(key, cs, vs) := if (cs == []) {
    stop("no pattern of the function matches")
    none
} else {
    l := arg(cs[0], 0)
    base := arg(cs[0], 1)
    rest := list.drop(cs, 1)
    if (arity(arg(l, 0)) != length(vs)) try(key, rest, vs)
    else {
        c := true
        i := 0
        for (v in vs) {
            k := i
            c = pe_and(c, () -> pe_test(arg(arg(l, 0), k), v))
            i = i + 1
        }
        go := () -> {
            env := pe_env(base)
            j := 0
            for (v in vs) {
                bind(env, arg(arg(l, 0), j), v)
                j = j + 1
            }
            sb := bodies
            bodies = arg(l, 1) :: bodies
            r := pe_eval(env, arg(l, 1))
            bodies = sb
            r
        }
        if (c == true) go()
        else if (c == false) try(key, rest, vs)
        else dyn_if(c, go, () -> try(key, rest, vs))
    }
}

unfold(key, cs, vs) := {
    saved := pe_stack
    pe_stack = Tuple{key, depth} :: pe_stack
    r := try(key, cs, vs)
    pe_stack = saved
    r
}

clauses_of(f) := map(l -> Tuple{l, root}, table.get(pe_defs, f, []))

# the function f of the tree called with the values vs: a call is made if f is being unfolded outside the branch of a dynamic condition around it
call_named(f, vs) := {
    if (find(fr -> arg(fr, 0) == f and arg(fr, 1) < depth, pe_stack) != none) residual_call(f, vs)
    else unfold(f, clauses_of(f), vs)
}

call_dynamic(fv, vs) := {
    ops := map(box_op, vs)
    assign(Val{}, Call{pe_at, arg(box(fv), 0), ops})
}

cl_key(fv) := arg(arg(fv, 0)[0], 0)

call_value(fv, vs) := match fv {
    Fv{f} -> call_named(f, vs)
  | Pr{f} -> primitive(f, vs)
  | Cl{cs, _} -> {
        key := cl_key(fv)
        if (find(fr -> arg(fr, 0) == key and arg(fr, 1) < depth, pe_stack) != none) call_dynamic(fv, vs)
        else unfold(key, cs, vs)
    }
  | Kn{k, hs, st} -> {
        sh := handlers
        ss := pe_stack
        handlers = hs
        pe_stack = st
        r := k(vs[0])
        handlers = sh
        pe_stack = ss
        r
    }
  | Ki{} -> vs[0]
  | Dy{_, Val{}} -> call_dynamic(fv, vs)
  | _ -> {
        stop("a value that is not a function is called")
        none
    }
}

var_value(Mt{x, t}) := assign(t, Mov{Reg{pe_at, x}})
var_value(Ce{c}) := assign(Val{}, Index{pe_at, arg(c, 0), Imm{pe_at, 0}})
var_value(v) := v

apply(env, f, vs) := if (typeof(f) == 'symbol) {
    loc := pe_loc(env, f)
    if (loc != none) call_value(var_value(table.get(env_vals(loc), f, none)), vs)
    else if (table.get(pe_defs, f, none) != none) call_named(f, vs)
    else primitive(f, vs)
} else call_value(pe_eval(env, f), vs)

# === Conditions ===
# the statements of fn() in the branch of a condition with the frame: Br{statements, value or Gone{}, Defs of the branch}. A Def of the branch
# is taken out of its environment; pe_put_defs puts it back after the condition.
branch(frame, fn) := {
    sf := frames
    so := opens
    ss := pe_stack
    sh := handlers
    sb := bodies
    sd := deflog
    sl := loops
    se := escapes
    escapes = []
    deflog = []
    frames = frame :: sf
    depth = depth + 1
    base := length(so)
    out := capture(() -> handle {
        v := fn()
        close(base, v)
    } with (PeAbort{}, k) -> {
        close_gone(base)
        Gone{}
    })
    depth = depth - 1
    frames = sf
    opens = so
    pe_stack = ss
    handlers = sh
    bodies = sb
    loops = sl
    defs := take_defs()
    deflog = sd
    esc := escapes
    escapes = se
    add_escapes(esc)
    Br{arg(out, 0), arg(out, 1), defs, esc}
}

add_escapes(hs) := for (h in hs) if (not list.any(x -> arg(x, 0) == arg(h, 0), escapes)) escapes = h :: escapes

# the Defs of the branch: Tuple{environment, name, value}, and the environments as they were before the branch
take_defs() := {
    seen := []
    out := []
    for (e in deflog) {
        env := arg(e, 0)
        x := arg(e, 1)
        if (not list.any(p -> arg(p, 0) == x and same_env(arg(p, 1), env), seen)) {
            seen = Tuple{x, env} :: seen
            out = Tuple{env, x, table.get(env_vals(env), x, none)} :: out
        }
        table.set(env_vals(env), x, arg(e, 2))
    }
    out
}

same_env(a, b) := arg(a, 0) == arg(b, 0)

# the statements to put before the condition of the frame
frame_pre(fr) := arg(fr, 1)[0]
new_frame() := Fr{depth + 1, {
    a := array(1)
    a[0] = []
    a
}}
add_pre(fr, s) := {
    a := arg(fr, 1)
    a[0] = append(a[0], s)
}
emit_pre(fr) := for (s in frame_pre(fr)) emit(s)

# the opens above base are ended: the value v of the path that went on is put in a register that both paths set
close(base, v) := {
    n := length(opens) - base
    if (n <= 0) v else {
        r := if (pe_dyn(v)) {
            t := arg(v, 1)
            x := fresh(t)
            emit(Assign{pe_at, x, Mov{operand(v)}})
            Dy{x, t}
        } else v
        close_opens(n, if (pe_dyn(r)) Tuple{arg(r, 0), arg(r, 1)} else none)
        r
    }
}

close_gone(base) := {
    n := length(opens) - base
    if (n > 0) close_opens(n, none)
}

# end n opens; the register holds the dummy on the paths that left
close_opens(n, reg) := {
    i := n
    while (i > 0) {
        o := opens[0]
        opens = list.drop(opens, 1)
        # a variable defined on the path that went on is read after the condition, so the other path sets it too
        dummies := []
        for (e in arg(o, 5)) {
            cur := table.get(env_vals(arg(e, 0)), arg(e, 1), none)
            if (pe_dyn(cur)) {
                y := fresh(arg(cur, 1))
                emit(Assign{pe_at, y, Mov{operand(cur)}})
                dummies = Assign{pe_at, y, Mov{dummy_op(arg(cur, 1))}} :: dummies
                table.set(env_vals(arg(e, 0)), arg(e, 1), Dy{y, arg(cur, 1)})
            }
        }
        inner := reverse(pe_stmts)
        pe_stmts = arg(o, 0)
        emit_pre(arg(o, 3))
        for (s in dummies) emit(s)
        if (i == 1 and reg != none) emit(Assign{pe_at, arg(reg, 0), Mov{dummy_op(arg(reg, 1))}})
        emit(if (arg(o, 4)) IfS{pe_at, Mov{arg(o, 1)}, arg(o, 2), inner} else IfS{pe_at, Mov{arg(o, 1)}, inner, arg(o, 2)})
        frames = list.drop(frames, 1)
        depth = depth - 1
        i = i - 1
    }
}

# go on in the path of a condition with the statements stmts, whose other path has left with the statements gone. gone_first: the left path is the then part.
open(c, gone, stmts, frame, defs, gone_first) := {
    opens = Op{pe_stmts, c, gone, frame, gone_first, defs} :: opens
    pe_stmts = reverse(stmts)
    frames = frame :: frames
    depth = depth + 1
}

# the handles hs that a path of the code left: the code from here runs when their flags are not set
check_escapes(hs) := {
    for (h in hs) {
        if (list.any(x -> arg(x, 0) == arg(h, 0), handlers)) {
            fl := arg(h, 3)[2]
            if (fl != none) open(Reg{pe_at, fl}, [], [], new_frame(), [], true)
        }
    }
}

# keys for comparing static values: a function made here is its lambdas
pe_key(v) := if (typeof(v) == 'mexpr) {
    if (head(v) == 'Cl) ClK{map(c -> arg(c, 0), arg(v, 0)), arg(v, 1)}
    else if (head(v) == 'Kn) KnK{}
    else foldl((t, x) -> push(t, x), mexpr(head(v), Tuple{}), map(pe_key, vasm_tlist(v)))
} else v

same_value(a, b) := pe_key(a) == pe_key(b)

set_at_end(stmts, r, t, v) := {
    saved := pe_stmts
    pe_stmts = reverse(stmts)
    set_reg(r, t, v)
    out := reverse(pe_stmts)
    pe_stmts = saved
    out
}

# if with a dynamic condition: both branches are evaluated, and the value is a variable that each branch sets
dyn_if(cv0, fa, fb) := {
    cv := truth(cv0)
    if (cv == true) fa()
    else if (cv == false) fb()
    else {
        c := operand(cv)
        frame := new_frame()
        ra := branch(frame, fa)
        rb := branch(frame, fb)
        sa := arg(ra, 0)
        sb := arg(rb, 0)
        va := arg(ra, 1)
        vb := arg(rb, 1)
        if (va == Gone{} and vb == Gone{}) {
            emit_pre(frame)
            emit(IfS{pe_at, Mov{c}, sa, sb})
            perform PeAbort{}
        } else if (va == Gone{}) {
            for (e in arg(rb, 2)) table.set(env_vals(arg(e, 0)), arg(e, 1), arg(e, 2))
            open(c, sa, sb, frame, arg(rb, 2), true)
            check_escapes(arg(rb, 3))
            vb
        } else if (vb == Gone{}) {
            for (e in arg(ra, 2)) table.set(env_vals(arg(e, 0)), arg(e, 1), arg(e, 2))
            open(c, sb, sa, frame, arg(ra, 2), false)
            check_escapes(arg(ra, 3))
            va
        } else {
            da := arg(ra, 2)
            db := arg(rb, 2)
            names := append(da, filter(e -> not list.any(p -> arg(p, 1) == arg(e, 1) and same_env(arg(p, 0), arg(e, 0)), da), db))
            for (e in names) {
                env := arg(e, 0)
                x := arg(e, 1)
                old := table.get(env_vals(env), x, none)
                fda := find(p -> arg(p, 1) == x and same_env(arg(p, 0), env), da)
                fdb := find(p -> arg(p, 1) == x and same_env(arg(p, 0), env), db)
                xa := if (fda == none) old else arg(fda, 2)
                xb := if (fdb == none) old else arg(fdb, 2)
                if (same_value(xa, xb) or pe_fun(xa) or pe_fun(xb)) table.set(env_vals(env), x, if (fda != none) xa else xb)
                else {
                    t := pe_join(kind_type(xa), kind_type(xb))
                    r := fresh(t)
                    sa = set_at_end(sa, r, t, xa)
                    sb = set_at_end(sb, r, t, xb)
                    table.set(env_vals(env), x, Dy{r, t})
                    table.set(env_depths(env), x, depth)
                }
            }
            esc := append(arg(ra, 3), arg(rb, 3))
            if (not opaque(va) and not opaque(vb) and va == vb) {
                emit_pre(frame)
                emit(IfS{pe_at, Mov{c}, sa, sb})
                check_escapes(esc)
                va
            } else if (pe_fun(va) and pe_fun(vb) and same_value(va, vb)) {
                emit_pre(frame)
                emit(IfS{pe_at, Mov{c}, sa, sb})
                check_escapes(esc)
                va
            } else {
                t := pe_join(kind_type(va), kind_type(vb))
                x := fresh(t)
                sa = set_at_end(sa, x, t, va)
                sb = set_at_end(sb, x, t, vb)
                emit_pre(frame)
                emit(IfS{pe_at, Mov{c}, sa, sb})
                check_escapes(esc)
                Dy{x, t}
            }
        }
    }
}

pe_if(env, c, a, b) := {
    cv := pe_eval(env, c)
    if (pe_dyn(cv)) dyn_if(cv, () -> pe_eval(env, a), () -> pe_eval(env, b))
    else if (cv != false) pe_eval(env, a)
    else pe_eval(env, b)
}

# === Assignments ===
# the frame of the depth d
frame_at(d) := find(fr -> arg(fr, 0) == d, frames)

# the location of x in the environment loc becomes a register, which holds the value of x from before the condition around it
make_mut(loc, x, v) := {
    cur := table.get(env_vals(loc), x, none)
    d := table.get(env_depths(loc), x, 0)
    t := if (forced(x)) Val{} else pe_join(kind_type(cur), kind_type(v))
    r := fresh(t)
    if (d < depth and frame_at(d + 1) != none) {
        fr := frame_at(d + 1)
        c := capture(() -> set_reg(r, t, cur))
        add_pre(fr, arg(c, 0))
    } else set_reg(r, t, cur)
    table.set(env_vals(loc), x, Mt{r, t})
    Mt{r, t}
}

assign_var(env, x, v) := {
    loc0 := pe_loc(env, x)
    loc := if (loc0 == none) root else loc0
    if (loc0 == none) {
        table.set(env_vals(root), x, none)
        table.set(env_depths(root), x, 0)
    }
    cur := table.get(env_vals(loc), x, none)
    match cur {
        Mt{r, t} -> {
            if (not fits(v, t)) widen(x)
            set_reg(r, t, v)
        }
      | Ce{c} -> emit(IStore{pe_at, arg(c, 0), Imm{pe_at, 0}, box_op(v)})
      | _ -> if (table.get(env_depths(loc), x, 0) >= depth) table.set(env_vals(loc), x, v)
        else {
            # a variable from outside a loop that is left is a register from the start of the loop
            if (list.any(l -> arg(l, 1) > table.get(env_depths(loc), x, 0), loops) and not forced(RegIn{x})) widen(RegIn{x})
            m := make_mut(loc, x, v)
            set_reg(arg(m, 0), arg(m, 1), v)
        }
    }
}

# === Loops ===
# the names assigned in the tree t
pe_assigned(t) := if (typeof(t) != 'mexpr) []
    else if (head(t) == 'Quote) []
    else {
        inner := concat_map(pe_assigned, vasm_tlist(t))
        if (head(t) == 'Set and typeof(arg(t, 0)) == 'symbol and not (typeof(arg(t, 1)) == 'mexpr and head(arg(t, 1)) == 'Fusion)) arg(t, 0) :: inner
        else inner
    }

# the symbols in the tree t
syms_into(t, out) := if (typeof(t) == 'symbol) table.set(out, t, true)
    else if (typeof(t) == 'mexpr and head(t) != 'Quote) each(x -> syms_into(x, out), vasm_tlist(t))

syms(t) := {
    out := table.new()
    syms_into(t, out)
    table.keys(out)
}

# the variables assigned in the tree of a loop are registers from before the loop
loop_regs(env, tree) := {
    names := pe_assigned(tree)
    extra := filter(x -> forced(RegIn{x}), syms(tree))
    for (x in append(names, extra)) {
        loc := pe_loc(env, x)
        if (loc != none) {
            cur := table.get(env_vals(loc), x, none)
            if (not (typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and (head(cur) == 'Mt or head(cur) == 'Ce))) make_mut(loc, x, cur)
        }
    }
}

# the value of the condition c when it depends on nothing dynamic now
static_cond(env, c) := {
    sd := decls
    ss := pe_stmts
    sn := count
    si := impls
    v := pe_eval(env, c)
    static := not opaque(v)
    decls = sd
    pe_stmts = ss
    count = sn
    impls = si
    if (static) (if (v != false) true else false) else none
}

pe_while(env, c, b) := {
    rounds := 0
    state := static_cond(env, c)
    while (state == true and rounds < loop_limit) {
        pe_eval(env, b)
        rounds = rounds + 1
        state = static_cond(env, c)
    }
    if (state == false) none
    else {
        loop_regs(env, Tuple{c, b})
        go := fresh(Bool{})
        cv := truth(pe_eval(env, c))
        emit(Assign{pe_at, go, Mov{if (pe_dyn(cv)) operand(cv) else Imm{pe_at, cv}}})
        frame := new_frame()
        sl := loops
        loops = Lp{go, depth + 1} :: loops
        r := branch(frame, () -> {
            pe_eval(env, b)
            cv2 := truth(pe_eval(env, c))
            emit(Assign{pe_at, go, Mov{if (pe_dyn(cv2)) operand(cv2) else Imm{pe_at, cv2}}})
            none
        })
        loops = sl
        emit_pre(frame)
        emit(WhileS{pe_at, Mov{Reg{pe_at, go}}, arg(r, 0)})
        check_escapes(arg(r, 3))
        none
    }
}

# === Handlers ===
# The state of a handle: an array of the register of its value, its type, and the register of its flag (set when a path has left it).
# A handler is Hd{id, function, depth, state, key}.

handler_clause(Cl{cs, _}, ev) := find(c -> {
    l := arg(c, 0)
    arity(arg(l, 0)) == 2 and static_match(arg(arg(l, 0), 0), ev) != false
}, cs)
handler_clause(_, ev) := none

# the pattern p matches v as far as it is known: true, false or 'dyn
static_match(p, v) := {
    t := typeof(p)
    if (t == 'symbol) (if (p == true or p == false or p == none) (if (opaque(v)) 'dyn else p == v) else true)
    else if (t == 'int or t == 'string) (if (opaque(v)) 'dyn else p == v)
    else if (head(p) == 'Quote) (if (opaque(v)) 'dyn else arg(p, 0) == v)
    else if (head(p) == '_TypeOf) 'dyn
    else if (val_dy(v)) 'dyn
    else if (not is_mexpr(v) or head(p) != head(v) or arity(p) != arity(v)) false
    else {
        r := true
        i := 0
        while (r != false and i < arity(p)) {
            m := static_match(arg(p, i), arg(v, i))
            if (m == false) r = false else if (m == 'dyn) r = 'dyn
            i = i + 1
        }
        r
    }
}

# the continuation k is the last thing that the tree of the handler does
k_tail(t, k) := if (not member(k, syms(t))) true else match t {
    Apply{f, Tuple{a}} -> f == k and not member(k, syms(a))
  | If{c, a, b} -> not member(k, syms(c)) and k_tail(a, k) and k_tail(b, k) and member(k, syms(a)) and member(k, syms(b))
  | Do{} -> false
  | _ -> if (head(t) == 'Do) {
        xs := vasm_tlist(t)
        list.all(x -> not member(k, syms(x)), list.take(xs, length(xs) - 1)) and k_tail(xs[length(xs) - 1], k)
    } else false
}

# leave the handle h with the value v from where the depth is more than that of the handle
abort(h, v) := {
    st := arg(h, 3)
    if (st[0] == none) {
        t := if (forced(arg(h, 4))) Val{} else kind_type(v)
        st[0] = fresh(t)
        st[1] = t
    }
    if (not fits(v, st[1])) widen(arg(h, 4))
    set_reg(st[0], st[1], v)
    if (st[2] == none) st[2] = fresh(Bool{})
    emit(Assign{pe_at, st[2], Mov{Imm{pe_at, true}}})
    for (l in loops) if (arg(l, 1) > arg(h, 2)) emit(Assign{pe_at, arg(l, 0), Mov{Imm{pe_at, false}}})
    if (not list.any(x -> arg(x, 0) == arg(h, 0), escapes)) escapes = h :: escapes
    perform PeAbort{}
}

pe_perform(ev) := {
    found := none
    for (h in handlers) if (found == none and handler_clause(arg(h, 1), ev) != none) found = h
    if (found == none) {
        stop("an effect has no handler in the function that is made")
        none
    } else if (arg(found, 2) == depth) perform PeEff{arg(found, 0), ev}
    else {
        c := handler_clause(arg(found, 1), ev)
        l := arg(c, 0)
        kp := arg(arg(l, 0), 1)
        sh := handlers
        handlers = list.drop(handlers, list.index_of(found, handlers) + 1)
        if (static_match(arg(arg(l, 0), 0), ev) == 'dyn) {
            handlers = sh
            stop("a handler whose pattern depends on a value known only when the program runs is not left in vasm")
            none
        } else if (typeof(kp) == 'symbol and not member(kp, syms(arg(l, 1)))) {
            v := unfold(l, [c], [ev, none])
            handlers = sh
            abort(found, v)
        } else if (typeof(kp) == 'symbol and k_tail(arg(l, 1), kp)) {
            v := unfold(l, [c], [ev, Ki{}])
            handlers = sh
            v
        } else {
            handlers = sh
            stop("a continuation that is not the last thing of the handler is not left across a condition known only when the program runs")
            none
        }
    }
}

# handle e with h
pe_handle(env, e, hexpr) := {
    hv := pe_eval(env, hexpr)
    nhandles = nhandles + 1
    id := nhandles
    st := array(3)
    h := Hd{id, hv, depth, st, HandleOf{hexpr}}
    sh := handlers
    sd := depth
    sst := pe_stack
    sbd := bodies
    sfr := frames
    start := pe_stmts
    base := length(opens)
    handlers = h :: sh
    v := handle {
        r := handle pe_eval(env, e) with (PeAbort{}, k) -> {
            close_gone(base)
            Gone{}
        }
        if (r == Gone{}) r
        else if (st[0] != none) {
            if (not fits(r, st[1])) widen(arg(h, 4))
            set_reg(st[0], st[1], r)
            close_gone(base)
            Gone{}
        } else close(base, r)
    } with (PeEff{i, ev}, k) -> {
        if (i == id) {
            hs := handlers
            stack := pe_stack
            handlers = sh
            call_value(hv, [ev, Kn{k, hs, stack}])
        } else k(perform PeEff{i, ev})
    }
    handlers = sh
    pe_stack = sst
    bodies = sbd
    depth = sd
    frames = sfr
    escapes = filter(x -> arg(x, 0) != id, escapes)
    if (st[0] != none) {
        # the register and the flag have values on all the paths
        new := list.take(pe_stmts, length(pe_stmts) - length(start))
        init := if (st[2] == none) [] else [Assign{pe_at, st[2], Mov{Imm{pe_at, false}}}]
        pe_stmts = append(new, append(init, Assign{pe_at, st[0], Mov{dummy_op(st[1])}} :: start))
        # the handler ran with its continuation and has its own value
        if (v != Gone{}) set_reg(st[0], st[1], v)
        check_escapes(escapes)
        Dy{st[0], st[1]}
    } else if (v == Gone{}) perform PeAbort{}
    else {
        check_escapes(escapes)
        v
    }
}

# === Quasi-quotes ===
quasi(env, t) := if (typeof(t) != 'mexpr) t
    else if (head(t) == 'UnQuote) pe_eval(env, arg(t, 0))
    else foldl((a, x) -> push(a, x), mexpr(head(t), Tuple{}), map(x -> quasi(env, x), vasm_tlist(t)))

# f | g
clauses_value(Cl{cs, _}) := cs
clauses_value(Fv{f}) := clauses_of(f)
clauses_value(_) := none

fusion(a, b) := if (a == none) b else {
    ca := clauses_value(a)
    cb := clauses_value(b)
    if (ca == none or cb == none) {
        stop("| of a function that is not made here is not left in vasm")
        b
    } else Cl{append(ca, cb), new_id()}
}

pe_eval(env, e) := {
    t := typeof(e)
    if (t == 'int or t == 'string) e
    else if (t == 'symbol) {
        loc := pe_loc(env, e)
        if (loc != none) var_value(table.get(env_vals(loc), e, none))
        else if (e == true or e == false or e == none) e
        else if (table.get(pe_defs, e, none) != none) Fv{e}
        else {
            g := eval(e)
            if (typeof(g) == 'function) Pr{e} else lift(g)
        }
    } else if (t != 'mexpr) e
    else if (head(e) == 'Quote) arg(e, 0)
    else if (head(e) == 'QuasiQuote) quasi(env, arg(e, 0))
    else if (head(e) == 'Apply) {
        f := lib_callee(env, arg(e, 0))
        args := arg(e, 1)
        if (f == '_index_get and arity(args) == 2 and argv_call(arg(args, 0))) argv_get(pe_eval(env, arg(args, 1)))
        else if (f == 'array_len and arity(args) == 1 and argv_call(arg(args, 0))) pe_argc()
        else if (typeof(f) == 'mexpr and head(f) == 'Quote) apply(env, arg(f, 0), values(env, args))
        else apply(env, f, values(env, args))
    } else if (head(e) == 'If) pe_if(env, arg(e, 0), arg(e, 1), arg(e, 2))
    else if (head(e) == 'While) pe_while(env, arg(e, 0), arg(e, 1))
    else if (head(e) == 'Lambda) Cl{[Tuple{e, env}], new_id()}
    else if (head(e) == 'Fusion) fusion(pe_eval(env, arg(e, 0)), pe_eval(env, arg(e, 1)))
    else if (head(e) == 'Do) {
        r := none
        for (x in vasm_tlist(e)) r = pe_eval(env, x)
        r
    } else if (head(e) == 'Def) {
        v := pe_eval(env, arg(e, 1))
        def(env, arg(e, 0), v)
        v
    } else if (head(e) == 'Declare) {
        if (table.get(env_vals(env), arg(e, 0), Unbound{}) == Unbound{}) def(env, arg(e, 0), none)
        none
    } else if (head(e) == 'Set) {
        v := pe_eval(env, arg(e, 1))
        assign_var(env, arg(e, 0), v)
        v
    } else if (head(e) == 'Handle) pe_handle(env, arg(e, 0), arg(e, 1))
    else if (head(e) == 'Perform) pe_perform(pe_eval(env, arg(e, 0)))
    else foldl((a, x) -> push(a, x), mexpr(head(e), Tuple{}), values(env, e))
}

# === Function values ===
# a function that is left as a value keeps the dynamic values that it uses. A variable that is assigned is shared with the place where the
# function was made, so it is an array of one element in both.

has_dy_deep(v, seen) := if (pe_dyn(v)) true
    else if (typeof(v) != 'mexpr) false
    else if (head(v) == 'Cl) {
        if (member(arg(v, 1), seen)) false
        else list.any(c -> list.any(x -> {
            loc := pe_loc(arg(c, 1), x)
            loc != none and loc_dy(table.get(env_vals(loc), x, none), arg(v, 1) :: seen)
        }, syms(arg(c, 0))), arg(v, 0))
    } else if (pe_fun(v)) head(v) == 'Kn or head(v) == 'Ki
    else list.any(x -> has_dy_deep(x, seen), vasm_tlist(v))

loc_dy(v, seen) := typeof(v) == 'mexpr and (head(v) == 'Mt or head(v) == 'Ce or has_dy_deep(v, seen))

# the location of x becomes an array of one element
make_cell(loc, x) := {
    cur := table.get(env_vals(loc), x, none)
    if (typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and head(cur) == 'Ce) cur
    else {
        d := table.get(env_depths(loc), x, 0)
        c := fresh(Val{})
        mk := () -> {
            emit(Assign{pe_at, c, Call{pe_at, 'array, [Imm{pe_at, 1}, Sym{pe_at, 'none}]}})
            emit(IStore{pe_at, c, Imm{pe_at, 0}, box_op(if (typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and head(cur) == 'Mt) Dy{arg(cur, 0), arg(cur, 1)} else cur)})
        }
        fr := frame_at(d + 1)
        if (d < depth and fr != none) add_pre(fr, arg(capture(mk), 0))
        else mk()
        if (d < depth and fr != none and typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and head(cur) == 'Mt) emit(IStore{pe_at, c, Imm{pe_at, 0}, box_op(Dy{arg(cur, 0), arg(cur, 1)})})
        cell := Ce{Dy{c, Val{}}}
        table.set(env_vals(loc), x, cell)
        cell
    }
}

boxing := []

box_fun(fv) := match fv {
    Fv{f} -> {
        val_of_function(fv, Tuple{'fnval, f}, arity(arg(table.get(pe_defs, f, [])[0], 0)))
    }
  | Pr{f} -> {
        cs := if (arity_known(f)) none else lib_clauses(f)
        if (cs != none) {
            table.set(pe_defs, f, cs)
            box_fun(Fv{f})
        } else val_of_function(fv, Tuple{'fnval, f}, arity_of(f))
    }
  | Cl{cs, _} -> box_closure(fv)
  | _ -> {
        stop("a continuation is not a value that is left in vasm")
        assign(Val{}, Mov{Sym{pe_at, 'none}})
    }
}

arity_known(f) := find(p -> arg(p, 0) == f, impl_table) != none or find(p -> arg(p, 0) == f, pe_ops) != none or f == 'println or f == '_not

# a function of vasm that takes and gives val for the function fv with n arguments
val_of_function(fv, key, n) := {
    hit := find(m -> arg(m, 0) == key, memo)
    name := if (hit != none) arg(hit, 1) else {
        nres = nres + 1
        nm := intern(f"{entry}_spec_{nres}")
        make_fn(nm, fv, map(_ -> Dyn{Val{}}, range(0, n)), 0, Val{}, key)
        nm
    }
    assign(Val{}, Clo{pe_at, name, []})
}

box_closure(fv) := {
    cs := arg(fv, 0)
    lams := map(c -> arg(c, 0), cs)
    if (member(lams, boxing)) {
        stop("functions that call each other as values with values known only when the program runs are not left in vasm")
        assign(Val{}, Mov{Sym{pe_at, 'none}})
    } else {
        names := syms(foldl((t, x) -> push(t, x), Tuple{}, lams))
        assigned := append(concat_map(pe_assigned, lams), concat_map(pe_assigned, bodies))
        env2 := En{table.new(), root, table.new(), 0}
        caps := []
        keys := []
        k := 0
        env0 := arg(cs[0], 1)
        for (x in names) {
            loc := pe_loc(env0, x)
            if (loc != none) {
                cur := table.get(env_vals(loc), x, none)
                isself := typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and head(cur) == 'Cl and map(c -> arg(c, 0), arg(cur, 0)) == lams
                if (isself) table.set(env_vals(env2), x, SelfRef{})
                else if (member(x, assigned) or (typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and head(cur) == 'Ce)) {
                    cell := make_cell(loc, x)
                    caps = arg(cell, 0) :: caps
                    table.set(env_vals(env2), x, Ce{Dy{intern(f"a{k}"), Val{}}})
                    keys = CellOf{x} :: keys
                    k = k + 1
                } else if (typeof(cur) == 'mexpr and head(cur) == 'Mt) {
                    caps = var_value(cur) :: caps
                    table.set(env_vals(env2), x, Dy{intern(f"a{k}"), Val{}})
                    keys = CapOf{x} :: keys
                    k = k + 1
                } else if (has_dy_deep(cur, [])) {
                    caps = cur :: caps
                    table.set(env_vals(env2), x, Dy{intern(f"a{k}"), Val{}})
                    keys = CapOf{x} :: keys
                    k = k + 1
                } else {
                    table.set(env_vals(env2), x, cur)
                    keys = Tuple{x, pe_key(cur)} :: keys
                }
            }
        }
        cs2 := map(c -> Tuple{arg(c, 0), env2}, cs)
        fv2 := Cl{cs2, new_id()}
        for (x in names) if (table.get(env_vals(env2), x, none) == SelfRef{}) table.set(env_vals(env2), x, fv2)
        key := Tuple{'closure, lams, keys}
        n := arity(arg(lams[0], 0))
        hit := find(m -> arg(m, 0) == key, memo)
        ops := map(box_op, reverse(caps))
        name := if (hit != none) arg(hit, 1) else {
            nres = nres + 1
            nm := intern(f"{entry}_spec_{nres}")
            sb := boxing
            boxing = lams :: sb
            make_fn(nm, fv2, map(_ -> Dyn{Val{}}, range(0, k + n)), k, Val{}, key)
            boxing = sb
            nm
        }
        assign(Val{}, Clo{pe_at, name, ops})
    }
}

# === The functions that are made ===

# the key of a call: the function and its arguments, each a static value or Dyn{type}. A value with a dynamic part is a val.
template(vs) := map(v -> if (pe_dyn(v)) Dyn{arg(v, 1)} else if (has_dy_deep(v, [])) Dyn{Val{}} else v, vs)

tmpl_key(tmpl) := map(pe_key, tmpl)

# the element of a template, the static value v of the call, as a parameter
dynamize(v, old) := if (marker(v)) v
    else if (marker(old)) old
    else Dyn{kind_type(v)}

# the template of a call whose static values differ from those of the function that is being made for the same function: the elements that
# differ are parameters
generalize(tmpl, old) := {
    out := []
    i := 0
    for (v in tmpl) {
        out = (if (pe_key(v) == pe_key(old[i])) v else dynamize(v, old[i])) :: out
        i = i + 1
    }
    reverse(out)
}

# the type of the result of a function made for the function fv
ret_type(f) := if (forced(Ret{f})) Val{}
    else if (Fv{f} == entry_fv) pe_rty
    else if (pe_rty == Unit{}) Val{}
    else pe_rty

# the call of the function f made for the static values of vs; the dynamic values of vs are its arguments
residual_call(f, vs) := {
    tmpl := template(vs)
    keyf := Fv{f}
    hit := find(m -> arg(m, 0) == Tuple{keyf, tmpl_key(tmpl)}, memo)
    if (hit == none) {
        outer := find(m -> arg(m, 0) == keyf and length(arg(m, 1)) == length(tmpl), making)
        if (outer != none) {
            tmpl = generalize(tmpl, arg(outer, 1))
            hit = find(m -> arg(m, 0) == Tuple{keyf, tmpl_key(tmpl)}, memo)
        }
    }
    ret := if (hit != none) arg(hit, 2) else ret_type(f)
    name := if (hit != none) arg(hit, 1) else {
        nres = nres + 1
        nm := intern(f"{entry}_spec_{nres}")
        make_fn(nm, keyf, tmpl, 0, ret, Tuple{keyf, tmpl_key(tmpl)})
        nm
    }
    args := []
    i := 0
    for (a in tmpl) {
        if (marker(a)) args = operand(coerce(vs[i], arg(a, 0))) :: args
        i = i + 1
    }
    args = reverse(args)
    if (ret == Unit{}) {
        emit(CallS{pe_at, name, args})
        none
    } else assign(ret, Call{pe_at, name, args})
}

# the variables that the statements read
reads_into(s, out) := if (typeof(s) == 'symbol) table.set(out, s, true)
    else if (typeof(s) == 'mexpr) match s {
        Decl{_, _, _} -> none
      | Assign{_, _, r} -> reads_into(r, out)
      | Cons{a, b} -> {
            reads_into(a, out)
            reads_into(b, out)
        }
      | _ -> each(x -> reads_into(x, out), vasm_tlist(s))
    }

pure(Mov{_}) := true
pure(Conv{_, _, Val{}}) := true
pure(Con{_, _, _}) := true
pure(Clo{_, _, _}) := true
pure(_) := false

# the assignments to variables that are not read, with no other effect, are taken out
clean_stmts(ss, reads) := concat_map(s -> match s {
    Assign{_, x, r} -> if (pure(r) and not table.get(reads, x, false)) [] else [s]
  | IfS{at, c, a, b} -> {
        a2 := clean_stmts(a, reads)
        b2 := clean_stmts(b, reads)
        if (a2 == [] and b2 == [] and head(c) == 'Mov) [] else [IfS{at, c, a2, b2}]
    }
  | WhileS{at, c, a} -> [WhileS{at, c, clean_stmts(a, reads)}]
  | _ -> [s]
}, ss)

clean(ss) := {
    reads := table.new()
    reads_into(ss, reads)
    out := clean_stmts(ss, reads)
    if (out == ss) out else clean(out)
}

# the statements of the function: the variables first
pe_body(r, ret) := {
    op := if (ret == Unit{}) none else operand(coerce(r, ret))
    ss := clean(append(reverse(pe_stmts), [Ret{pe_at, op}]))
    reads := table.new()
    reads_into(ss, reads)
    assigned := table.new()
    assigns_into(ss, assigned)
    append(filter((Decl{_, x, _}) -> table.get(reads, x, false) or table.get(assigned, x, false), reverse(decls)), ss)
}

assigns_into(ss, out) := each(s -> match s {
    Assign{_, x, _} -> table.set(out, x, true)
  | IfS{_, _, a, b} -> {
        assigns_into(a, out)
        assigns_into(b, out)
    }
  | WhileS{_, _, a} -> assigns_into(a, out)
  | _ -> none
}, ss)

# the function name of vasm for the function fv called with tmpl, whose elements are static values or Dyn{type}.
# The first skip parameters are not arguments of fv: the environment of fv has them. key is what the function is kept under.
make_fn(name, fv, tmpl, skip, ret, key) := {
    memo = Tuple{key, name, ret} :: memo
    making = Tuple{fv, tmpl} :: making
    sd := decls
    ss := pe_stmts
    sc := count
    sdp := depth
    sst := pe_stack
    sfr := frames
    sop := opens
    shd := handlers
    slp := loops
    sec := escapes
    sdl := deflog
    sbd := bodies
    sar := arrays
    arrays = []
    decls = []
    pe_stmts = []
    count = 0
    depth = 0
    pe_stack = []
    frames = []
    opens = []
    handlers = []
    loops = []
    escapes = []
    deflog = []
    bodies = []
    ps := []
    vs := []
    i := 0
    for (a in tmpl) {
        if (marker(a)) {
            x := intern(f"a{i}")
            ps = Param{pe_at, x, arg(a, 0)} :: ps
            if (i >= skip) vs = Dy{x, arg(a, 0)} :: vs
        } else if (i >= skip) vs = lift(a) :: vs
        i = i + 1
    }
    vs = reverse(vs)
    r := handle match fv {
        Fv{f} -> unfold(f, clauses_of(f), vs)
      | Cl{cs, _} -> unfold(cl_key(fv), cs, vs)
      | Pr{f} -> primitive(f, vs)
    } with (PeAbort{}, k) -> none
    # a function other than the first has the type val when its value does not fit
    if (ret != Unit{} and not fits(r, ret) and key != first_key) match fv {
        Fv{f} -> widen(Ret{f})
      | _ -> none
    }
    d := Fn{pe_at, name, [], reverse(ps), ret, pe_body(r, ret)}
    decls = sd
    pe_stmts = ss
    count = sc
    depth = sdp
    pe_stack = sst
    frames = sfr
    opens = sop
    handlers = shd
    loops = slp
    escapes = sec
    deflog = sdl
    bodies = sbd
    arrays = sar
    making = list.drop(making, 1)
    pe_fns = d :: pe_fns
    name
}


# the functions of vasm/builtins.pk that the functions fs call, with the functions that these call
calls_into(s, out) := if (typeof(s) == 'mexpr) match s {
    Call{_, f, a} -> {
        table.set(out, f, true)
        calls_into(a, out)
    }
  | CallS{_, f, a} -> {
        table.set(out, f, true)
        calls_into(a, out)
    }
  | _ -> each(x -> calls_into(x, out), vasm_tlist(s))
}

impl_closure(names) := {
    all_impls := arg(vasm_planck.builtins, 0)
    need := table.new()
    work := names
    while (work != []) {
        f := work[0]
        work = list.drop(work, 1)
        if (not table.get(need, f, false)) {
            table.set(need, f, true)
            d := find(x -> arg(x, 1) == f, all_impls)
            if (d != none) {
                out := table.new()
                calls_into(arg(d, 5), out)
                work = append(table.keys(out), work)
            }
        }
    }
    filter(d -> table.get(need, arg(d, 1), false), all_impls)
}

# the module of vasm for the function of the tree called with args (static values and Dyn{type}), whose result has the type rty
export specialize(tree, args, rty) := {
    if (not is_fun_tree(tree)) panic("partial_eval: the first argument of specialize is the tree of a function")
    force = table.new()
    result := none
    while (result == none) {
        result = handle specialize_once(tree, args, rty) with (PeRestart{}, k) -> none
    }
    result
}

specialize_once(tree, args, rty) := {
    pe_defs = table.new()
    decls = []
    pe_stmts = []
    count = 0
    depth = 0
    pe_stack = []
    frames = []
    opens = []
    handlers = []
    loops = []
    escapes = []
    deflog = []
    bodies = []
    pe_rty = rty
    pe_fns = []
    memo = []
    impls = []
    nres = 0
    making = []
    boxing = []
    root = En{table.new(), none, table.new(), 0}
    fv := fun_value(tree)
    entry_fv = fv
    entry = match fv {
        Fv{f} -> symname(f)
      | _ -> "lambda"
    }
    tmpl := map(a -> if (marker(a)) a else if (is_fun_tree(a)) fun_value(a) else a, args)
    first_key = Tuple{pe_key(fv), tmpl_key(tmpl)}
    make_fn(intern(f"{entry}_spec"), fv, tmpl, 0, rty, first_key)
    made := map(m -> find(d -> arg(d, 1) == arg(m, 1), pe_fns), reverse(memo))
    Module{append(made, impl_closure(reverse(impls)))}
}

# the module m of specialize with the function main that calls its first function with the values vs (static values of planck).
# A result of an integer type or bool is the status of main; a result of another type is printed.
export with_main(m, vs) := {
    f := arg(arg(m, 0)[0], 1)
    ps := arg(arg(m, 0)[0], 3)
    rty := arg(arg(m, 0)[0], 4)
    decls = []
    pe_stmts = []
    count = 0
    impls = []
    pe_fns = []
    memo = []
    making = []
    frames = []
    depth = 0
    regs := []
    i := 0
    for (p in ps) {
        regs = operand(coerce(vs[i], arg(p, 2))) :: regs
        i = i + 1
    }
    args := reverse(regs)
    ints := vasm_check.int(rty) or rty == Bool{}
    body := if (ints) {
        set_reg_call(f, args, rty)
    } else if (rty == Unit{}) {
        emit(CallS{pe_at, f, args})
        emit(Ret{pe_at, none})
    } else {
        r := assign(rty, Call{pe_at, f, args})
        pe_println(if (rty == Val{} or ref_dy(r) or vasm_check.int(rty)) r else none)
        emit(Ret{pe_at, none})
    }
    fns := append(reverse(pe_fns), [Fn{pe_at, 'main, [], [], if (ints) rty else Unit{}, append(reverse(decls), reverse(pe_stmts))}])
    have := map(d -> arg(d, 1), arg(m, 0))
    extra := filter(d -> not member(arg(d, 1), have), impl_closure(impls))
    Module{append(arg(m, 0), append(extra, fns))}
}

set_reg_call(f, args, rty) := {
    r := assign(rty, Call{pe_at, f, args})
    emit(Ret{pe_at, operand(r)})
}

# the module m as the text of vasm; the function main of with_main is not in it. The name vasm_text of the field is also the name of the
# library outside, so the library is held in text_of_vasm before the body defines its own vasm_text.
export vasm_text(m) := text_of_vasm(Module{filter(d -> arg(d, 1) != 'main, arg(m, 0))})
}
